<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you enter is stored.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>The two-check system</h2>
<p>Replacement cost value (RCV) is what it costs to repair or replace with like kind and quality today. Actual cash value (ACV) is RCV minus depreciation. Many policies pay ACV minus the deductible first, then pay the withheld depreciation once you complete repairs within the policy’s time limit.</p>
<h2>How depreciation is estimated here</h2>
<p>The tool uses straight-line depreciation: age divided by expected life, applied to the replacement cost and capped at the percentage you choose. Real estimates may use different life tables, condition adjustments or non-depreciable items such as labor in some cases. Use the result to understand the carrier’s math, not to replace it.</p>
<h2>What to check on your own estimate</h2>
<ul>
<li>Is depreciation applied to labor, and does your policy allow it?</li>
<li>Are the ages and life expectancies reasonable for your materials?</li>
<li>Is the depreciation marked recoverable or non-recoverable?</li>
<li>How many days do you have to complete repairs and claim the holdback?</li>
</ul>
<h2>Questions about this worksheet</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is recoverable depreciation?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It’s the depreciation withheld from your first payment that you can collect after completing repairs, if your policy pays replacement cost.</p></div></details><details><summary>Why does the tool cap depreciation?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Estimates rarely depreciate items to zero. Many cap at a percentage. Choose the cap that matches your estimate.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if my policy is ACV only?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Tick the box. The tool will show that no holdback is recoverable and the total equals ACV minus the deductible.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free worksheets</h2><div class="cards cards-3"><a class="card card-tool rv" href="/claim-worksheets/roof-pitch-and-squares-calculator/"><span class="card-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roofer-at-work.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roofer-at-work-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roofer-at-work.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="802" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="card-tag">Calculator</span></span><span class="card-body"><h3 class="card-t">Roof Pitch &amp; Squares Calculator</h3><span cla